@* Shown to a tenant user who signed in successfully but holds neither portal app role. Naming the
   roles is deliberate: the fix is an Entra group assignment, so the message must say what to ask for
   (portal-auth spec: "denies access with a message naming the required roles").

   This renders its own h1 inside the page well rather than through PortalSections.PageHeader: the
   topbar sections are filled by routed pages, and this component replaces the page rather than being
   one. Routes.razor still finds an h1 to focus. *@
<h1 class="page-title-row" style="margin:0 0 var(--sp-1)">No portal access</h1>

<div class="banner">
    <span class="banner-icon">
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
             stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" />
            <path d="M12 8v4M12 16h.01" />
        </svg>
    </span>
    <span>
        You are signed in as <strong>@AccountName</strong>, but this account holds neither portal role,
        so no stack data is shown.
    </span>
</div>

<div class="card" style="max-width:640px">
    <div class="card-head">
        <h2>Ask for one of these in Entra ID</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <dl class="dl" style="grid-template-columns:auto 1fr">
            <dt><span class="badge neutral mono">@PortalRoles.Reader</span></dt>
            <dd>Read every view.</dd>
            <dt><span class="badge info mono">@PortalRoles.Operator</span></dt>
            <dd>Read, plus retry, cancel, and manual dispatch.</dd>
        </dl>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    private Task<AuthenticationState>? AuthenticationState { get; set; }

    string AccountName { get; set; } = "unknown";

    protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync()
    {
        if (AuthenticationState is not null)
        {
            var state = await AuthenticationState;
            AccountName = state.User.Identity?.Name ?? "unknown";
        }
    }
}
